WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:03.033
-Drew, welcome to the show.
Come on.

00:00:03.033 --> 00:00:04.868
Can you be cooler?
Can you be cooler?

00:00:04.868 --> 00:00:06.901
There's no cool like you.
-I can't believe nobody's

00:00:06.901 --> 00:00:09.234
worn this sweatshirt
all this time.

00:00:09.234 --> 00:00:10.667
No one rocks it like you.

00:00:10.667 --> 00:00:12.200
I mean, look at the shoes,
everything.

00:00:12.200 --> 00:00:13.334
You know how to do it.
Come on, bud.

00:00:13.334 --> 00:00:15.067
-Shoe, pink lip.
-The pink lip.

00:00:15.067 --> 00:00:16.534
You know the deal.

00:00:16.534 --> 00:00:19.100
I got to say, you know, I watch
your show every single day.

00:00:19.100 --> 00:00:20.868
I love it.
Congrats on that.

00:00:20.868 --> 00:00:24.400
"The Drew Barrymore Show"
is awesome, and I -- It's --

00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:26.734
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Thank you.

00:00:26.734 --> 00:00:28.534
-I love it, I love --
There's so many things about it

00:00:28.534 --> 00:00:31.400
I love, but it was your birthday
the other day. Happy belated.

00:00:31.400 --> 00:00:34.667
-Thank you -- 2/22/22.
-Two two two two two two two.

00:00:34.667 --> 00:00:37.000
-It's so crazy.
I --

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:40.033
I mean, like,
I was born in '75 --

00:00:40.033 --> 00:00:43.067
1975.
-Yeah, of course.

00:00:43.067 --> 00:00:45.901
-And you just don't even think
about that future date.

00:00:45.901 --> 00:00:48.601
Like, it's --
it's almost a surreal thing.

00:00:48.601 --> 00:00:51.133
-Yeah.
-Like the year 2000 seemed nuts.

00:00:51.133 --> 00:00:53.400
Remember, we were all going
to party like it's 1999.

00:00:53.400 --> 00:00:54.968
It just, you know --
-Yeah, Y2K, man.

00:00:54.968 --> 00:00:57.467
-I never thought I'd get here,
and I've been looking so forward

00:00:57.467 --> 00:01:00.334
to that auspicious number
of a day

00:01:00.334 --> 00:01:02.501
that we'll kind of only see
once in our lifetime.

00:01:02.501 --> 00:01:04.334
-But then you actually
were hosting your show

00:01:04.334 --> 00:01:05.968
on your birthday?
-I was!

00:01:05.968 --> 00:01:08.334
Which is so happy because I got
to wake up with the kids,

00:01:08.334 --> 00:01:12.400
and then I got to go to work and
our job, our work environment --

00:01:12.400 --> 00:01:15.701
you guys know it's a family.
It's positive.

00:01:15.701 --> 00:01:18.334
It's like the rest of, you know,
your problems

00:01:18.334 --> 00:01:21.801
kind of dissipate and fade away
when you go to work

00:01:21.801 --> 00:01:24.667
because we're all working
on something so positive

00:01:24.667 --> 00:01:27.834
and multifaceted
and that feed our souls.

00:01:27.834 --> 00:01:30.868
And then I got to go home
after work, and I walked in,

00:01:30.868 --> 00:01:33.400
and there was a blindfold
taped to the door and --

00:01:33.400 --> 00:01:36.667
My daughters had put up there.
-Okay.

00:01:36.667 --> 00:01:38.334
Thank you for clearing that up.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:38.334 --> 00:01:41.234
-And I put it on, and I'm led in
by my daughters,

00:01:41.234 --> 00:01:43.567
and Olive learned to play
"Happy Birthday"

00:01:43.567 --> 00:01:44.834
for me on the piano.

00:01:44.834 --> 00:01:48.400
She's in lessons, but she taught
herself by herself.

00:01:48.400 --> 00:01:50.267
-Come on.
-And then Frankie --

00:01:50.267 --> 00:01:53.067
And they got me
a Fudgie the Whale cake.

00:01:53.067 --> 00:01:54.934
-Carvel!
Fudgie the Whale's the best!

00:01:54.934 --> 00:01:56.567
-It's the greatest!
-It's the greatest cake.

00:01:56.567 --> 00:01:58.267
-And they made me
beaded necklaces.

00:01:58.267 --> 00:02:00.167
And then our dog, Lucy --

00:02:00.167 --> 00:02:03.601
And, you know, Gary and Lucy
are, like, twinning.

00:02:03.601 --> 00:02:05.968
And -- And then
Lucy jumped on the cake

00:02:05.968 --> 00:02:07.234
and started eating
the whole thing.

00:02:07.234 --> 00:02:09.334
And dogs cannot have chocolate.
-Of course.

00:02:09.334 --> 00:02:11.801
-So within a matter
of just a minute,

00:02:11.801 --> 00:02:13.868
the whole place looked nuts.
-Chaos.

00:02:13.868 --> 00:02:15.767
-And I was like, "This is
the best birthday ever."

00:02:15.767 --> 00:02:17.434
-Yeah, of course, dude!
That's the best. Why not?

00:02:17.434 --> 00:02:19.667
-That's it.
-I was watching your show

00:02:19.667 --> 00:02:20.834
because I was like,
they were celebrating you

00:02:20.834 --> 00:02:22.667
on your show,
and then you got a surprise

00:02:22.667 --> 00:02:25.367
from The Go-Go's,
and they came on.

00:02:25.367 --> 00:02:27.501
They Zoomed on together,
and they gave you this.

00:02:27.501 --> 00:02:29.734
They made you an honorary Go-Go.

00:02:29.734 --> 00:02:32.000
-I mean, that's me.
-That's Drew.

00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:34.133
They -- They --
-I mean --

00:02:34.133 --> 00:02:36.501
-They made this for me,

00:02:36.501 --> 00:02:38.801
and because I went
and I inducted them

00:02:38.801 --> 00:02:40.667
into the Rock and Roll
Hall of Fame.

00:02:40.667 --> 00:02:42.167
Here's -- I have
a photo of that, by the way.

00:02:42.167 --> 00:02:43.901
This is you doing --
This was genius.

00:02:43.901 --> 00:02:46.534
You did this
as you were intro'ing them.

00:02:46.534 --> 00:02:48.834
You started putting on,
you know, a night mask,

00:02:48.834 --> 00:02:50.801
whatever,
a towel over your head.

00:02:50.801 --> 00:02:54.133
It felt sort of like, "Okay.
These are the women that,

00:02:54.133 --> 00:02:55.434
when they came into my life,

00:02:55.434 --> 00:02:58.367
when I was about 6 years old,
they told me,

00:02:58.367 --> 00:03:00.601
'You can do anything you want.
You can --'"

00:03:00.601 --> 00:03:02.801
I mean, Nan and I made
"Charlie's Angels."

00:03:02.801 --> 00:03:04.934
I don't think I would have dared
make a "Charlie's Angels"

00:03:04.934 --> 00:03:06.400
if it wasn't for The Go-Go's.

00:03:06.400 --> 00:03:08.033
And what I loved is,
they didn't say,

00:03:08.033 --> 00:03:09.801
"You have to pretend
to be a man."

00:03:09.801 --> 00:03:11.234
You get to be
with your girlfriends

00:03:11.234 --> 00:03:13.534
and do everything you dream.

00:03:13.534 --> 00:03:17.000
And it was the best sort of
tone-setter for my entire life.

00:03:17.000 --> 00:03:21.200
So I was like, "How do I pay
these women in the right way?"

00:03:21.200 --> 00:03:22.467
And I just thought,
"I'm gonna go back to

00:03:22.467 --> 00:03:25.000
when I was a little girl,
saw that album cover,

00:03:25.000 --> 00:03:27.934
and it changed my life forever,"
and I put the mask on.

00:03:27.934 --> 00:03:29.801
-It was the best moment of the
Rock and Roll Hall of Fame.

00:03:29.801 --> 00:03:31.801
-Oh, my God! Thank you!
I was so nervous.

00:03:31.801 --> 00:03:34.067
-Questlove was there,
and I got a text from him,

00:03:34.067 --> 00:03:36.334
he said, "Yo, your girl
is crushing it right now."

00:03:36.334 --> 00:03:37.734
-I'm so relieved.
-And I was like, "What?

00:03:37.734 --> 00:03:39.634
What is she doing?" He's like,
"Just wait till you see.

00:03:39.634 --> 00:03:41.467
She's intro'ing The Go-Go's,
and it's brilliant."

00:03:41.467 --> 00:03:42.868
-Oh, my God,
I felt so much pressure

00:03:42.868 --> 00:03:44.200
to get that moment right.

00:03:44.200 --> 00:03:48.701
How do you say to someone
or a group of people,

00:03:48.701 --> 00:03:50.901
"My life changed
because of you"?

00:03:50.901 --> 00:03:52.534
And the whole trajectory,
I know,

00:03:52.534 --> 00:03:56.934
ties back to seeing these girls
that just --

00:03:56.934 --> 00:03:58.868
There was
such a wow factor to me.

00:03:58.868 --> 00:04:00.834
It was like The Go-Go's
and Pippi Longstocking

00:04:00.834 --> 00:04:03.234
are my DNA.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:03.234 --> 00:04:05.334
-Pippi Longstocking, of course.
-Of course.

00:04:05.334 --> 00:04:07.968
Girls who were girls
who can do anything.

00:04:07.968 --> 00:04:09.934
I told you already this,
but I loved your interview

00:04:09.934 --> 00:04:11.801
with Donny Osmond.
I thought it was awesome.

00:04:11.801 --> 00:04:13.801
I love Donny Osmond. I was like,
"Dude, it was great."

00:04:13.801 --> 00:04:15.767
You were just great
and asked some great questions.

00:04:15.767 --> 00:04:17.868
That's the part of your show
that I love the best

00:04:17.868 --> 00:04:19.501
because you ask questions,
they're like...

00:04:19.501 --> 00:04:20.901
A lot of the times,
they're like,

00:04:20.901 --> 00:04:23.133
"That's the best question.
No one's ever asked me that."

00:04:23.133 --> 00:04:24.434
-Thank you.
-And I love that you do that.

00:04:24.434 --> 00:04:26.367
Yeah, I love it.
-I was freaked out

00:04:26.367 --> 00:04:28.634
for your interview
with Dua last night.

00:04:28.634 --> 00:04:30.067
-That was.
-That's my pal.

00:04:30.067 --> 00:04:35.367
-That was a breakdown
of humanity and experience

00:04:35.367 --> 00:04:36.968
and "These are the things
I've learned,

00:04:36.968 --> 00:04:38.400
and this is how I've grown."

00:04:38.400 --> 00:04:41.000
It was so informative.
-Dua Lipeeps.

00:04:41.000 --> 00:04:44.734
-I already am, like,
psychotically obsessed with her,

00:04:44.734 --> 00:04:46.534
and now I'm like,
"Oh, no. How --"

00:04:46.534 --> 00:04:47.801
-She's actually cooler
than you even understand.

00:04:47.801 --> 00:04:49.133
-It hurts.
-It actually hurts.

00:04:49.133 --> 00:04:52.601
-But it was great to hear her
talk about real stuff.

00:04:52.601 --> 00:04:53.934
-Yeah.
-You know?

00:04:53.934 --> 00:04:55.300
That's what we want to do --
we want to have fun

00:04:55.300 --> 00:04:56.601
and lean into comedy,

00:04:56.601 --> 00:04:58.567
but I need to get real
every once in a while

00:04:58.567 --> 00:05:00.100
because it's not all...

00:05:00.100 --> 00:05:01.968
-That's why people love you.
-Oh. God.

00:05:01.968 --> 00:05:05.234
-Yeah, because, no, it's good.
You get -- You get emotional.

00:05:05.234 --> 00:05:07.234
You're not afraid
to do any of that stuff.

00:05:07.234 --> 00:05:10.033
-I -- I know our tone
of the show is weird,

00:05:10.033 --> 00:05:12.734
but I'm weird,
and I -- I like comedy.

00:05:12.734 --> 00:05:14.534
It's medicine to me.
I like news.

00:05:14.534 --> 00:05:20.033
I like, you know, food
and design and human interest

00:05:20.033 --> 00:05:22.167
and conversations
and seeing somebody

00:05:22.167 --> 00:05:24.267
you've loved your whole life
walk out and be like,

00:05:24.267 --> 00:05:27.067
"Oh, my God," and someone
you had never met before,

00:05:27.067 --> 00:05:29.868
but you will always remember
them after hearing their story.

00:05:29.868 --> 00:05:31.167
Everybody has a story.

00:05:31.167 --> 00:05:32.400
-Everyone's got a story, yeah.

00:05:32.400 --> 00:05:34.133
And I want to talk more.
-Okay!

00:05:34.133 --> 00:05:36.133
-More with Drew Barrymore
when we come back.

